# Data — never commit satellite products
data/nisar_l2/*
data/dem/*
data/slc/*
!data/**/.gitkeep
*.h5
*.zip
*.SAFE/
*.tif
*.tiff

# Outputs
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep

# Bulk products of a run: never useful to anyone else, always regenerable in
# seconds from files that ARE committed.
*.png
*.csv

# ...except the documentation figures. The README embeds these, so a blanket
# *.png rule leaves every image on the front page broken on GitHub while it
# looks perfect locally - nobody notices until someone opens the repository.
# This is the same way the source-zone results went missing in 4fc6518, and
# it is worth a rule rather than a second rediscovery.
!docs/figures/*.png
!docs/*.png

# ...except the derived measurements. These are a few kilobytes each and
# they are the scientific result: every statistic, time series and noise
# floor the analysis rests on. Regenerating one means re-downloading a
# gigabyte per pair, so they belong in version control even though the
# products they came from never can.
#
# These negations must come AFTER the blanket *.csv above, not before it -
# git applies the last matching pattern, so the order was silently ignoring
# all of them. The committed files survived only because they were already
# tracked, which would not have helped a fresh clone.
!outputs/*stats*.csv
!outputs/ts_*.csv
!outputs/detectability.csv
# The same sweep under the old flat gate. Keeping it is what makes the
# correction checkable rather than asserted.
!outputs/detectability_fixed_gate.csv
# Same reasoning for the impoundment maps: 13 KB each, and regenerating one
# means several thousand external DEM queries.
!outputs/dam_sites_*.geojson
# And the per-pair elevation fits: they are the evidence for limitation 4.
!outputs/troposphere_*.csv
# And the point-versus-area floors: they are the evidence for the headline bound.
!outputs/local_floor_*.csv
# The candidate table, the common-datum run and the headline built from them.
!outputs/scar_candidates_source.csv
!outputs/common_ref_*.csv
!outputs/bound_source.csv

# Secrets
.env
.netrc
_netrc

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

review/

# Interactive site build caches. Regenerated by docs/site/build_data.py; the
# grid cache in particular is a 6 MB npz of the Sentinel-2 difference.
docs/site/_*_cache.json
docs/site/_*_cache.npz
